  "question": "You are given a list of integers representing the daily prices of a stock over $n$ days. You are also given an integer $k$. Find the $k$ most expensive distinct stock prices from the list, sorted in descending order.",
  "function_name": "top_k_distinct_prices",
  "signature": "def top_k_distinct_prices(prices: list[int], k: int) -> list[int]",
  "checker": "exact",
  "reference_solution": "import heapq\n\ndef top_k_distinct_prices(prices: list[int], k: int) -> list[int]:\n    unique_prices = list(set(prices))\n    min_heap = []\n    for price in unique_prices:\n        if len(min_heap) < k:\n            heapq.heappush(min_heap, price)\n        elif price > min_heap[0]:\n            heapq.heapreplace(min_heap, price)\n    return sorted(min_heap, reverse=True)",
